### Runnable in IntelliJ / VS Code REST Client. Replace the IDs after each step.
@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Create two users
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@example.com", "name": "Alice", "phoneNumber": "9876543210" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "bob@example.com", "name": "Bob" }

### 2. Create a wallet for each (paste user ids)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "ALICE_USER_ID", "currency": "INR" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/wallets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "BOB_USER_ID", "currency": "INR" }

### 3. Fund Alice
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/deposit
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: dep-0001

{ "toWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "amount": 1000.00, "description": "Initial top-up" }

### 4. Transfer Alice -> Bob (run twice: second call returns 200 with replayed=true)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/transfer
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-0001

{ "fromWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "toWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 250.50, "description": "Dinner" }

### 5. Same key, different amount -> 422 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_ERROR
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/transfer
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-0001

{ "fromWalletId": "ALICE_WALLET_ID", "toWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 999.00 }

### 6. Overdraw -> 422 INSUFFICIENT_FUNDS (and the same on retry with tx-0002)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/transactions/withdraw
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-0002

{ "fromWalletId": "BOB_WALLET_ID", "amount": 5000.00 }

### 7. Inspect
GET {{host}}/api/v1/wallets/ALICE_WALLET_ID/balance

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/wallets/ALICE_WALLET_ID/ledger

###
GET {{host}}/api/v1/wallets/BOB_WALLET_ID/transactions
